<title>USA: TABLE - Seacoast Q2 oper shr lower.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Seacoast Q2 oper shr lower.</headline>
<dateline>STUART, Fla 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Net shr		    $0.28		    $0.47</p>
<p> Oper shr		    0.45		     0.47</p>
<p> Net			  1,437		    2,440</p>
<p> Oper net		   2,365		    2,440</p>
<p> Net int. income	  9,647		    9,062</p>
<p>	  6   MONTHS</p>
<p> Net shr		    $0.71		    $0.93</p>
<p> Oper shr		    0.89		     0.93</p>
<p> Net			  3,697		    4,789</p>
<p> Oper net		   4,672		    4,789</p>
<p> Net int. income	 19,206		   18,048</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	     388			397</p>
<p> Total assets	   869,882		  826,567</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers. Return in equity is in percent.)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Seacoast Banking Corp of Florida.</p>
<p>Oper income figures are before merger-related expenses of $1,467,000 ($926,000 after tax) for second quarter and $75,000 ($47,000 after tax) for first quarter.</p>
<p>Net interest income is on a fully taxable equivalent basis.</p>
<p>1997 Q2 net shr includes a $928,000, or $0.17-per-share, after-tax charge related to the termination of certain contracts, a consolidation of facilities and other one-time expenses related to a merger.</p>
